**Describe the issue**
All of the cht-core defined widgets have this factory loader syntax around them. [Example](https://github.com/medic/cht-core/blob/master/webapp/src/js/enketo/widgets.js#L1). From what I can tell, this appears to be on cht-core widgets only and not on the enketo-core widgets.

```
if ( typeof exports === 'object' && typeof exports.nodeName !== 'string' && typeof define !== 'function' ) {
  var define = function( factory ) { // eslint-disable-line
    factory( require, exports, module );
  };
}
```

This wrapper prevents the widgets from being built using webpack. This makes supporting our custom enketo widgets in the medic-conf-test-harness more difficult. https://github.com/medic/medic-conf-test-harness/issues/46

I suspect this may block the upgrade to a modern angular build system with tree shaking (haven't investigated, just a guess).

**Describe the improvement you'd like**
Can we safely remove this wrapper?
